<http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P49715>
        a       owl:Class .

gomodel:6ab067da00001778
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "Revision: HRAS -> MAP3K1 and MAP2K3 -> MAPK13 changed to 'directly positively regulates' with has_input. HRAS-GTP binds the MEKK1 kinase domain directly (PMID:7744823; mouse MEKK1, hence ISS with MGI:MGI:1346872); MKK3 phosphorylates/activates p38delta (IDA PMID:9374491, PMID:9790884). PKCdelta -> HRAS, MAP3K1 -> MAP2K3 (no evidence that MEKK1 directly phosphorylates MKK3; MEKK1's documented substrates are MKK4/7/MEK1) and MAPK13 -> CEBPA remain 'causally upstream of, positive effect'." , "Curator decision: the PTH2R-Gs (GNAS) arm (PMID:34353904, HEK293T/cryo-EM) was removed from this model because it has no downstream components and no keratinocyte evidence; better captured as standard PTH2R annotations. MEK3 (MAP2K3) and p38delta (MAPK13) units occur in keratinocyte (PMID:12080077)." , "IVL arm added: PTH2R (PLC pathway unit) causally upstream of PKCdelta (IC: TIP39 raises involucrin via PTH2R, PMID:27000502; calcium-induced involucrin requires PKCdelta, PMID:11864971; with GO:0007200) -> HRAS -> MAP3K1 (MEKK1) -> MAP2K3 (MEK3) -> MAPK13 (p38delta) -> CEBPA -> IVL, from dominant-negative epistasis in human keratinocytes (PMID:12080077, abstract only). Intra-cascade edges are 'causally upstream of, positive effect' because direct mechanisms were not shown; p38delta is reported to be activated by MKK6 in vitro (PMID:9218798). HRAS chosen for generic dominant-negative Ras. The PTH2R->PKCdelta join is a curator inference, not tested for TIP39. KRT14 arm not modelled (no evidence linking Ca2+/PKC to loss of deltaNp63)." , "Human TIP39 (PTH2) acting from the extracellular region on PTH2R in epidermal keratinocytes, increasing cytosolic Ca2+ from ER stores via a PLC/IP3R-dependent route and promoting keratinocyte differentiation (PMID:27000502, PMID:28094886; ligand-receptor activation PMID:34353904). Gq, PLC and IP3R isoforms are not identified in the source papers (pharmacological inhibitors only) and are therefore not modelled. GO:0005576 used because GO:0005615 extracellular space is obsolete (replaced_by GO:0005576)." , "Localization: p38delta (MAPK13) placed in nucleus per PMID:15340077 (p38delta-ERK1/2 complex relocates to the keratinocyte nucleus in response to PKCdelta; abstract only, survival/death context). MEK3 (MAP2K3) placed in cytoplasm with TAS PMID:8622669 only; no experimental localization found." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. Human TIP39 (PTH2) activates PTH2R in keratinocytes, raising cytosolic Ca2+ via PLC signaling and promoting keratinocyte differentiation." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "development" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-01" ;
        dc:title               "TIP39-PTH2R signaling, keratinocyte differentiation (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "https://www.uniprot.org" , "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00001778 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

